      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone who runs and otherwise plays at music events on the regular, the ability to open an instance and *ensure staff are the first ones in there* is sorely needed, particularly in worlds that don't have whitelisting. \n\n- This would probably go along with the fact I'd love instance joinability settings to be adjustable without having to close it down and open a new one. \n\n- on that note, being able to designating a new instance owner before leaving would be lovely",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-17T02:52:22.386Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "・Request\n\nWhen creating a group + instance within a group, enable settings to allow specific roles to join in advance.\n\nWe would like only users with specific roles to be able to join until a designated time, after which all users can join.\n\n・Reason\n\nDuring events, there are times when we wish to gather beforehand.\n\nUntil now, we have often gathered in a separate instance, but moving instances resets the placement of drawings, objects, etc.\n\nIf gathering and going live could occur within the same instance, this would be highly beneficial for various events—inviting guests, preparing corporate representatives, and more.\n\n・Examples\n\nAt music events, performers often gather beforehand for sound checks.\n\nThis feature would prove invaluable in such scenarios.\n\nAt exhibition events, corporate representatives sometimes wish to observe actual user traffic.\n\nIf they could participate beforehand and observe people actually entering and enjoying the space, it would likely increase corporate satisfaction.\n\nFor networking events, staff may require time for meetings.\n\nAllocating staff meeting time within the hosted instance would facilitate smoother event operations and enhance user satisfaction.\n\nOverall, I felt it would be beneficial as it would make it easier for influential guests, such as streamers, to participate, thereby increasing VRChat's exposure.\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
